export default {"id":"production-level-7","number":7,"title":"Module 7 — Session Labs: 140, DnB, and Melodic","skillBand":"Textbook","duration":"From the course textbook","summary":"These two are the course’s heavy electronic labs (matching the Drums syllabus bias). Still skippable. No wub / LFO design. No Amen micro-edits.","modules":[{"id":"production-m-7-1","code":"7","title":"Dubstep / 140 and Drum & Bass labs (skippable)","blurb":"These two are the course’s heavy electronic labs (matching the Drums syllabus bias). Still skippable. No wub / LFO design. No Amen micro-edits.","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"production-l-o-10","title":"Section overview","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"overview","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"Module 7A — Dubstep / 140 and Drum & Bass labs (skippable)","level":1},{"type":"prose","html":"These two are the course’s <strong>heavy</strong> electronic labs (matching the Drums syllabus bias). Still skippable. No wub / LFO design. No Amen micro-edits."},{"type":"heading","text":"Section 7.1 — G-DUB · Dubstep / 140 (skippable)","level":1},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Topics:</strong> Local KB scenes; Beat Kitchen 3–5 min pop-like drop form. Snare-on-3 as <strong>section feel</strong>. Drop = texture/energy shift. Space between 1 and 3 is the arrangement."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-1-1","title":"7.1.1 — Intro–build–drop–mid–drop–outro","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.1.1 — Intro–build–drop–mid–drop–outro","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Intro–build–drop–mid–drop–outro.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"Beat Kitchen: dubstep arrangement is <strong>pop-shaped</strong> (intro–build–drop–breakdown–second build–second drop–outro), often 3–5 minutes. Local beginner KB performs the same arc as Session names (6.1.6)."},{"type":"prose","html":"Drop here = <strong>texture/energy shift</strong> (0.9.4), not house’s “groove returns.”"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> Your list has two drops or you wrote why the sketch has one."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-1-2","title":"7.1.2 — 140 template if local KB cited; other numbers exist","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.1.2 — 140 template if local KB cited; other numbers exist","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> 140 template if local KB cited; other numbers exist.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"Local <em>Dubstep-Production-Beginner</em> KB: typical band <strong>~132–142</strong>; most modern practice clusters at <strong>140</strong> (the nickname “140”). Template tempo <strong>140.00</strong>."},{"type":"prose","html":"Beat Kitchen (L0): <strong>135–145</strong>, center 140.   <em>How To Make Dubstep (UK_140)</em>: treat as form/UK-lane companion, not a second invented number."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>140 is not physics.</strong> Other 140-family tempos exist. If you leave 140, cite the local template. If you pick 138, say it is still inside 132–142."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> Tempo citation is local KB and/or Beat Kitchen, not “everyone knows.”"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-1-3","title":"7.1.3 — Berklee Now 140 / 4/4 beside the local band","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.1.3 — Berklee Now 140 / 4/4 beside the local band","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Berklee Now 140 / 4/4 beside the local band.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"Berklee Now, <em>Electronic Music Genres</em> (11 Apr 2025): <strong>Dubstep — 140 BPM | 4/4 time</strong>. They also name half-time and double-time <em>feel</em> inside that tempo."},{"type":"prose","html":"Write both on the sketch note:"},{"type":"list","items":["Local: ~132–142 / template 140  ","Berklee Now: 140 / 4/4  "],"ordered":false},{"type":"prose","html":"Agreement is useful. It still is not a law of nature."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> Both citations appear in the Project note."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-1-4","title":"7.1.4 — Build scene vs drop scene — what you remove","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.1.4 — Build scene vs drop scene — what you remove","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> What you <em>remove</em>.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"A 140 build often <strong>takes away</strong> the thing the drop will slam (bass weight, snare-on-3 identity, the chop). Then the drop <strong>returns it transformed</strong> — texture shift."},{"type":"prose","html":"Launch <code>02_Build</code>: fewer clips, plus a riser/silence (0.9.6). <code>03_Drop_A</code>: the missing weight is back, and something is <em>different</em> (a new bass clip, a new chop). Do not design a wobble."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> You can list what the build removed."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-1-5","title":"7.1.5 — Space between 1 and 3 is the arrangement","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.1.5 — Space between 1 and 3 is the arrangement","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Space between 1 and 3 is the arrangement.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"Local KB grid: kick on <strong>1</strong>, snare on <strong>3</strong> at 140. Beat Kitchen: dubstep <strong>lives in the gaps</strong>. The arrangement is what you <em>do not</em> put between those hits — not a 32nd-hat thesis."},{"type":"prose","html":"If the drop is full of busy percussion, you may have written trap-house. Leave air. That air is the section."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> A bar of the drop has audible space between 1 and 3."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-1-6","title":"7.1.6 — Local scene names …","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.1.6 — Local scene names …","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Local scene names <code>01_Intro</code> … <code>07_Outro</code>.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"Local KB §4.4 (8-bar thinking):"},{"type":"list","items":["<code>01_Intro</code>  ","<code>02_Build</code>  ","<code>03_Drop_A</code>  ","<code>04_Drop_B</code>  ","<code>05_Mid</code>  ","<code>06_Drop_2</code>  ","<code>07_Outro</code>  "],"ordered":true},{"type":"prose","html":"Use these names in this lab even if you skip <code>04</code> or <code>06</code>. Numbered prefixes sort in Session. They are <strong>local convention</strong>, not Ableton law."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> The seven names exist as rows (empty rows allowed)."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-1-7","title":"7.1.7 — Second drop = same form, one clip swapped","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.1.7 — Second drop = same form, one clip swapped","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Second drop = same form, one clip swapped.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"<code>06_Drop_2</code> = <code>03_Drop_A</code> with one clip changed. Same half-time identity. Variation, not a new genre."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> One-clip diff."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-1-8","title":"7.1.8 — Fake-out: build that becomes a breakdown","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.1.8 — Fake-out: build that becomes a breakdown","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Fake-out: build that becomes a breakdown.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"Beat Kitchen (0.9.6): a <strong>fake</strong> build that becomes a breakdown. Scene <code>02_Build</code> can launch into <code>05_Mid</code> (stripped) instead of <code>03_Drop_A</code>. Then drop later."},{"type":"prose","html":"Use once. Predictable fake-outs stop working."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> You performed one fake-out, or wrote “no fake-out this sketch.”"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-1-9","title":"7.1.9 — MK4: launch build → drop","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.1.9 — MK4: launch build → drop","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> On the Launchkey MK4 61: launch build → drop.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"Clip mode. Wait for an 8-bar wall if you can. The launch <em>is</em> the drop. Hands, not a mouse, if the MK4 is present."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> The texture change happens on a launch, not on a hidden Follow Action you forgot."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-1-10","title":"7.1.10 — Chops as mid-section glue (production, not wub)","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.1.10 — Chops as mid-section glue (production, not wub)","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Chops as mid-section glue (production, not wub).  "},{"type":"prose","html":"<code>05_Mid</code>: sliced legal phrase (1.4) as the thing that holds the ear while bass and snare rest. Production — re-order, reverse, re-pitch. Not LFO bass design (Sound Design / mustNotCover)."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> Mid scene is held by a chop clip, not a new Operator patch."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-1-11","title":"7.1.11 — 32–64 bar 140 sketch","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.1.11 — 32–64 bar 140 sketch","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> 32–64 bar 140 sketch.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"8-bar cells × 4 to 8 scenes. Listen file <code>LAB_140_sketch.wav</code>. Not a 3–5 minute single unless you want extra."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> Snare-on-3 appears in a drop scene."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-1-12","title":"7.1.12 — Written energy curve","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.1.12 — Written energy curve","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Written energy curve.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"Draw the 140 rollercoaster: low intro, climb, spike, mid valley, second spike, outro. Label scene numbers on the spikes."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Section 7.1 checkpoint:</strong> Drop means the world changed. You did not open a wub tutorial."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-2-1","title":"7.2.1 — DJ-friendly intro (32-bar option on cheat sheet)","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.2.1 — DJ-friendly intro (32-bar option on cheat sheet)","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> DJ-friendly intro (32-bar option on cheat sheet).  "},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>DNB Cheat Sheet</em> arrangement example starts <strong>DJ Intro (32 bars)</strong> → Breakdown 16–32 → Drop 16–32 → Drop Variation → Breakdown → Drop → Outro 16–32."},{"type":"prose","html":"Your 64-bar sketch cannot hold a full cheat-sheet single. Use <strong>16 or 32</strong> intro bars if you can; if the sketch is only 64 total, an 8- or 16-bar intro is an honest shrink — write <code>sketch-scale</code>."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> Intro is a mix-in corridor, not a pop hook fragment (unless you labeled a radio edit)."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-2-2","title":"7.2.2 — Cited tempo band 170–180 / 174–175","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.2.2 — Cited tempo band 170–180 / 174–175","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Cited tempo band 170–180 / 174–175.  "},{"type":"table","headers":["Source","Band"],"rows":[["<em>DNB Cheat Sheet</em>","<strong>170–180</strong>; usually <strong>174–175</strong>"],["Berklee Now (2025)","DnB <strong>160–180</strong>, 4/4 or 6/8"],["Beat Kitchen (L0 table)","use the cheat sheet / Berklee pair; do not invent a third center"]],"caption":null},{"type":"prose","html":"Beginner default for this lab: <strong>174</strong> or <strong>175</strong> from the cheat sheet. Berklee’s 160–180 is wider (includes some jungle/liquid edges). Show both; pick inside the cheat sheet unless you write a Berklee-justified 170."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> Tempo is 174 or 175, or a written citation for another number in 170–180."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-2-3","title":"7.2.3 — Breakdown vs drop as drum-section energy","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.2.3 — Breakdown vs drop as drum-section energy","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Breakdown vs drop as drum-section energy.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"Beat Kitchen: DnB energy often moves by <strong>section density</strong> — how much drum/break information is present. Breakdown: drums thin or gone, pads/vocal. Drop: kick/snare/break <strong>return</strong> at full density."},{"type":"prose","html":"This is closer to house “groove returns” than to a 140 texture planet — but the <em>drums</em> are the planet."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> Drop is denser in the drum column than the breakdown. One sentence."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-2-4","title":"7.2.4 — Place a chopped break clip in one scene only","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.2.4 — Place a chopped break clip in one scene only","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Place a chopped break clip in one scene only.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"If you sliced a <strong>legal</strong> break in 1.4, put that MIDI/Rack clip in the <strong>drop</strong> scene only. Breakdown stays without it. That single placement <em>is</em> arrangement."},{"type":"prose","html":"Do not open the Amen microscope (ghost notes, micro-edits). Drums course owns that."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> The break clip does not play in <code>Break</code>."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-2-5","title":"7.2.5 — Liquid vs jump-up form (space vs punch) — one sentence each","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.2.5 — Liquid vs jump-up form (space vs punch) — one sentence each","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> One sentence each.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"Cheat sheet lists Liquid and Jump Up as subgenres; instruments: “melodic for liquid/dancefloor, spooky for neuro/jump up.”"},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Form-only (this lab):</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Liquid:</strong> more space, longer pad/vocal beds, density changes are gentler.  ","<strong>Jump-up:</strong> punchier drop contrast; more “on/off” between break and drop."],"ordered":false},{"type":"prose","html":"Pick one sentence-pair and one lane for the sketch. No Reese-design class (cheat sheet mentions Reese as sound, not this homework)."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> Two sentences in the note. Sketch follows one lane."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-2-6","title":"7.2.6 — Amen as a clip you already own, not a science lab","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.2.6 — Amen as a clip you already own, not a science lab","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Amen as a <em>clip you already own</em>, not a science lab.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"Cheat sheet “common breakbeats: Amen, Think, Apache.” <em>Drum Breaks</em> history is real. <strong>This school’s rule (1.6):</strong> only if you <strong>already own</strong> a licensed/royalty-free version, or you skip Amen and use another legal break."},{"type":"prose","html":"Do not rip “Amen Brother.” Do not spend the lab slicing individual ghosts."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> Break source is in the source log, or you used a Core Library / RF break instead."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-2-7","title":"7.2.7 — Second drop / switch-up scene","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.2.7 — Second drop / switch-up scene","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Second drop / switch-up scene.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"Cheat sheet: Drop Variation 16–32. One clip swapped (a different break chop, a bass rest pattern). <code>Drop_2</code> / <code>Switch</code>."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> One-clip diff."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-2-8","title":"7.2.8 — MK4 launch","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.2.8 — MK4 launch","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> MK4 launch.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"Clip mode: <code>Break</code> → <code>Drop</code> at a cell wall. Optional Drum mode to play the chopped break <em>as</em> the drop if you performed it (1.4.10 cousin)."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> Density change is audible on launch."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-2-9","title":"7.2.9 — 64-bar DnB sketch","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.2.9 — 64-bar DnB sketch","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> 64-bar DnB sketch.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"Example: 16 intro + 16 break + 16 drop + 16 drop_var. Listen file <code>LAB_dnb_sketch.wav</code>. Tempo cited."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> 64 bars at a cited DnB tempo."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-2-10","title":"7.2.10 — Written density map","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.2.10 — Written density map","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Written density map.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"Per scene: low / mid / high <strong>drum density</strong>. That is the energy curve for this lab."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Section 7.2 checkpoint:</strong> You treated the break as a clip, not a doctoral thesis."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources for Module 6A (author-facing)","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Local <em>Dubstep-Production-Beginner-Live12-Launchkey.md</em> (132–142 / 140; scenes <code>01_Intro</code>–<code>07_Outro</code>; snare on 3)  ","Beat Kitchen dubstep form + gaps  ","Berklee Now (2025) dubstep 140/4/4; DnB 160–180  ","<em>DNB Cheat Sheet</em> (170–180 / 174–175; 32-bar DJ intro; Amen listed)  ","<em>How To Make Drum &amp; Bass</em> form pages (companion)  ","1.4 / 1.6 legality"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]},{"id":"production-m-7-2","code":"7","title":"Future bass, lo-fi, reggae/dub, ambient (skippable)","blurb":"Lighter labs. Still skippable. Same seven-step pedagogy. No vinyl-plugin course. No reggae history dissertation — clock and form only.","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"production-l-o-11","title":"Section overview","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"overview","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"Module 7B — Future bass, lo-fi, reggae/dub, ambient (skippable)","level":1},{"type":"prose","html":"Lighter labs. Still skippable. Same seven-step pedagogy. No vinyl-plugin course. No reggae history dissertation — clock and form only."},{"type":"heading","text":"Section 7.3 — G-FB · Future bass / melodic (skippable)","level":1},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Sources:</strong> <em>How to Make Future Bass like Flume in 5 Easy Steps</em>; Beat Kitchen overlap (half-time + bright chords)."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-3-1","title":"7.3.1 — Pop hook + club drop","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.3.1 — Pop hook + club drop","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Pop hook + club drop.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"Future bass sits on <strong>both clocks</strong>: a singable hook (0.4–0.8) and a <strong>drop</strong> that behaves like 140/trap (texture/energy, often half-time)."},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>How to Make Future Bass</em>: drums often kick on 1s, snare on 3s (half-time); their example project <strong>146 BPM</strong>; they state the genre “tends to sit from around <strong>145 to sometimes 160</strong>,” “a little faster than traditional dubstep (more in the 140–150 range).” Cite that band if you need a number. Do not invent 150 as a school default."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> You can point at a hook scene <em>and</em> a drop scene."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-3-2","title":"7.3.2 — Scene map","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.3.2 — Scene map","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Scene map.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"Suggested: <code>Intro</code> · <code>Verse</code> · <code>Build</code> · <code>Drop</code> · <code>Verse_2</code> or <code>Break</code> · <code>Drop_2</code>. Hook clip may live in verse (topline) and return over the drop, or the drop may be instrumental."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> Names, not <code>scene 3</code>."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-3-3","title":"7.3.3 — Chord Map on MK4 for the bed (recording, not theory)","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.3.3 — Chord Map on MK4 for the bed (recording, not theory)","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Chord Map on MK4 for the bed (recording, not theory).  "},{"type":"prose","html":"Novation MK4 <strong>Chord Map</strong> is a performance layer: hold a pad/key, the keyboard outputs a stored voicing. Use it to <strong>record a bed clip</strong> into <code>Verse</code> or <code>Drop</code>."},{"type":"prose","html":"This is not a harmony exam. Do not name scale degrees unless you already know them from Piano. If Chord Map is confusing, play a stock chord clip with two fingers and move on."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> A chord bed exists as a recorded clip, however you got the notes."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-3-4","title":"7.3.4 — Contrast verse softness vs drop density","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.3.4 — Contrast verse softness vs drop density","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Contrast verse softness vs drop density.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"Two levers (KB §9.4): verse = fewer clips, lower velocity, maybe no snare-on-3. Drop = hat/perc density + the half-time grid + the hook or a new lead clip. Stock sounds. <em>How to Make Future Bass</em> spends pages on layered kicks — <strong>not</strong> this lab. Place stock drums."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> Verse is softer <em>and</em> thinner than drop."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-3-5","title":"7.3.5 — Half-time + bright chords as a form hint","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.3.5 — Half-time + bright chords as a form hint","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Half-time + bright chords as a <em>form hint</em>.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"Beat Kitchen overlap note (syllabus): half-time drums + bright chord bed is a <strong>form hint</strong> that you are in this lane, not a synth recipe. If both are present, a listener can classify the drop without a wobble."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> Drop has snare-on-3 <em>and</em> a bright-ish chord clip (stock keys/Electric)."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-3-6","title":"7.3.6 — Second drop variation","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.3.6 — Second drop variation","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Second drop variation.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"One clip swapped. Same half-time identity."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> One-clip diff."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-3-7","title":"7.3.7 — 32-bar sketch","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.3.7 — 32-bar sketch","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> 32-bar sketch.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"Example: 8 verse + 8 build + 8 drop + 8 drop_2. Listen file <code>LAB_fb_sketch.wav</code>."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> 32 bars. Hook still identifiable or you wrote “instrumental drop.”"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-3-8","title":"7.3.8 — Written section list","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.3.8 — Written section list","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Written section list.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"Order you actually launched."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Section 7.3 checkpoint:</strong> Pop hook and club drop both exist as scenes."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-4-1","title":"7.4.1 — Short loops; less “drop”","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.4.1 — Short loops; less “drop”","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Short loops; less “drop”.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"Beat Kitchen: lo-fi / beat-tape thinking is <strong>loop and texture</strong>, not a cinematic drop. Cousin of boom-bap’s engine (4.1) without the 16/8 obligation."},{"type":"prose","html":"If you write a 140-style build-drop, you left the lab."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> No scene is named <code>Drop</code> unless you wrote why you broke the lane."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-4-2","title":"7.4.2 — Tempo: Beat Kitchen 70–90 or","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.4.2 — Tempo: Beat Kitchen 70–90 or","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Tempo: Beat Kitchen 70–90 or <code>gap</code>.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"L0 table: Beat Kitchen lo-fi <strong>70–90</strong>, center <strong>80</strong>. Cite that or leave the number out (<code>gap</code> / tap). Do not steal 85–96 from melodigging boom-bap unless you are actually in 4.1."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> 70–90 with citation, or no genre BPM claim."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-4-3","title":"7.4.3 — Variation by filter/clip length, not a new chorus","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.4.3 — Variation by filter/clip length, not a new chorus","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Variation by filter/clip length, not a new chorus.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"Two scenes, same loop: one filtered, one longer/shorter clip, or a layer muted. That is the “arrangement.” Everett chorus tests do not apply."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> Variation is a clip property, not a new topline."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-4-4","title":"7.4.4 — Imperfection as arrangement (not a vinyl-plugin course)","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.4.4 — Imperfection as arrangement (not a vinyl-plugin course)","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Imperfection as arrangement (not a vinyl-plugin course).  "},{"type":"prose","html":"Leave a late hat. Leave Warp off on a phrase (1.3). A little noise bed from a legal recording. Do <strong>not</strong> spend the lab shopping vinyl emulations or Redux as a personality."},{"type":"prose","html":"Imperfection is a <strong>decision you can point at</strong>."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> One intentional “wrong” timing or texture, written down."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-4-5","title":"7.4.5 — Tape-side: 32 bars, two variations","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.4.5 — Tape-side: 32 bars, two variations","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Tape-side: 32 bars, two variations.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"Think cassette side: one idea, two costumes, 32 bars total. <code>Loop_A</code> 16 + <code>Loop_B</code> 16."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> Two variations, one idea."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-4-6","title":"7.4.6 — Pad chops","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.4.6 — Pad chops","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Pad chops.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"MK4 Drum mode: a legal phrase on a few pads, played loosely. Capture. Channel 10, 36–51, MPE off."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> A chop clip exists. Source logged."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-4-7","title":"7.4.7 — 32-bar tape","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.4.7 — 32-bar tape","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> 32-bar tape.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"Listen file <code>LAB_lofi_tape.wav</code>."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> 32 bars. No fake drop."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-4-8","title":"7.4.8 — Written variation list","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.4.8 — Written variation list","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Written variation list.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"<code>A = loop dry</code> / <code>B = filter + one mute</code>."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Section 7.4 checkpoint:</strong> You varied without a chorus."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-5-1","title":"7.5.1 — Offbeat as the section identity","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.5.1 — Offbeat as the section identity","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Offbeat as the section identity.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"The <strong>skank</strong> (guitar/keys on the offbeats) <em>is</em> the section, the way snare-on-3 is 140’s section feel. Stock keys, offbeat clip. Drums stay light. Do not write a one-drop doctoral paper."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> Mute the offbeat clip and the genre identity collapses."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-5-2","title":"7.5.2 — Delay throws as arrangement (clip launch)","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.5.2 — Delay throws as arrangement (clip launch)","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Delay throws as arrangement (clip launch).  "},{"type":"prose","html":"A <strong>throw</strong> is a send/delay you <em>launch</em> as a scene (or a clip that is just a shouted/hummed word into Live’s <strong>Delay</strong> — owned, not Echo/Suite). The throw is a <strong>section event</strong>, like a fill."},{"type":"prose","html":"Do not design a dub delay plugin. Stock Delay, long feedback, you launch it, you stop it."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> There is a scene whose job is “the throw happens.”"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-5-3","title":"7.5.3 — Why UK bass music inherited this clock","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.5.3 — Why UK bass music inherited this clock","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Why UK bass music inherited this clock.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"Berklee Now (2025): jungle / DnB “rooted in Jamaican traditions such as <strong>reggae and dub</strong>” plus breakbeat experiment; dubstep later drew on that rhythmic/bass lineage."},{"type":"prose","html":"The inherited <strong>clock</strong> for this course: space, subtractive mixes, echo as a performer, offbeat identity. That is why 6.1’s gaps and 6.2’s density maps feel related. You are not required to write a lineage essay beyond this paragraph."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> One sentence: UK bass kept dub’s <em>space and echo-as-form</em>."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-5-4","title":"7.5.4 — Dub as subtractive form (strip, then throw)","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.5.4 — Dub as subtractive form (strip, then throw)","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Dub as subtractive form (strip, then throw).  "},{"type":"prose","html":"Full riddim, then <strong>strip</strong> (mute bass or drums), then a <strong>throw</strong>. Same family as techno mute maps (5.2) and house subtract (5.1.5), with echo as the paint."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> A stripped scene exists <em>and</em> a throw scene exists."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-5-5","title":"7.5.5 — Scene: full riddim vs stripped dub","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.5.5 — Scene: full riddim vs stripped dub","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Scene: full riddim vs stripped dub.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"<code>Riddim</code> = offbeat + bass + drums. <code>Dub</code> = stops on two of those + delay throw. Launch between them."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> Two rows, obvious subtract."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-5-6","title":"7.5.6 — MK4: launch the throw scene","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.5.6 — MK4: launch the throw scene","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> On the Launchkey MK4 61: launch the throw scene.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"Clip mode. The throw should be a <strong>launch</strong>, not a hidden automation you cannot perform."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> Hands fire the throw."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-5-7","title":"7.5.7 — 32-bar sketch","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.5.7 — 32-bar sketch","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> 32-bar sketch.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"16 riddim + 8 dub + 8 riddim (or similar). Listen file <code>LAB_reg_sketch.wav</code>. Tempo: do not invent. Use a tempo from an owned reggae/dub record you tap, or leave unlabeled."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> 32 bars. Offbeat identity holds."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-5-8","title":"7.5.8 — Written strip/add list","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.5.8 — Written strip/add list","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Written strip/add list.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"Per scene: what left, what entered, where the throw sits."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Section 7.5 checkpoint:</strong> Dub is subtract + throw, not a new synth."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-6-1","title":"7.6.1 — Evolution replaces chorus","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.6.1 — Evolution replaces chorus","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Evolution replaces chorus.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"Beat Kitchen ambient lane: there is often <strong>no chorus</strong>. The piece changes by <strong>evolution</strong> — a filter opens, a layer fades, a clip lengthens. Everett’s unvaried text does not apply."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> You cannot find a chorus and that is correct."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-6-2","title":"7.6.2 — Scenes as textures, not hooks","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.6.2 — Scenes as textures, not hooks","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Scenes as textures, not hooks.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"Name rows <code>Bed_A</code> · <code>Bed_B</code> · <code>Thin</code> · <code>Swell</code> — jobs of texture. A hummed hook is allowed as <em>color</em>, not as a title-line contract."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> No row is named <code>Chorus</code>."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-6-3","title":"7.6.3 — No drop required","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.6.3 — No drop required","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> No drop required.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"If you add a 140 drop, you left the lab. Plateau (5.2.5 cousin) or a slow swell is enough."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> Energy curve has no spike labeled drop."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-6-4","title":"7.6.4 — Long clips vs many scenes","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.6.4 — Long clips vs many scenes","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Long clips vs many scenes.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"Two legal architectures:"},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Few long clips</strong> (32-bar audio beds, Warp off or Texture mode from 1.2).  ","<strong>Many scenes</strong> that slowly add/subtract the same beds."],"ordered":false},{"type":"prose","html":"Pick one. Do not make 16 one-bar scenes."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> You can say which architecture you used."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-6-5","title":"7.6.5 — 32–64 bar bed","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.6.5 — 32–64 bar bed","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> 32–64 bar bed.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"Listen file <code>LAB_ambient_bed.wav</code>. Stock pads, legal field recording, or an unwarped phrase."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Check:</strong> The file exists and does not contain a snare-on-3 drop."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"production-l6-6-6","title":"7.6.6 — Written evolution notes","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"7.6.6 — Written evolution notes","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Short description:</strong> Written evolution notes.  "},{"type":"prose","html":"“Bar 17 filter opens.” “Bar 33 minus keys.” That page is the form."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Section 7.6 checkpoint:</strong> Evolution replaced chorus. You can read the notes without hearing a hook."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Sources for Module 6B (author-facing)","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["<em>How to Make Future Bass like Flume in 5 Easy Steps</em> (145–160; example 146; kick 1 / snare 3)  ","Beat Kitchen lo-fi 70–90 center 80; ambient evolution; overlap note for future bass  ","Berklee Now (2025) jungle/DnB ← reggae/dub lineage  ","Novation MK4 Chord Map (performance, not theory)  ","Live Delay (Standard) for throws — not Echo"],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]}]};
